# env files
# Deny every variant, then re-admit the two committed templates by name.
# The previous pair (`.env` + `.env*.local`) only caught those exact shapes:
# `.env.prod`, `.env.production` and `.env.development` were all committable,
# and those are precisely the names someone reaches for when they are about to
# write production values into a file. Deny-all-then-allow means a new name
# nobody predicted is ignored by default rather than committed by default.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.local.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# Audit/debug scratch. An agent auditing this app as a signed-in user mints a
# real NextAuth session JWT here (signed with NEXTAUTH_SECRET, valid for days)
# so it can click through the product the way a customer does. That token is a
# live credential for whoever's account it was minted for — it must never be
# committed, and neither should the scripts that mint it.
.audit-scratch/

# Screenshots taken to check a screen before shipping it (design-to-code:
# "a design you haven't looked at is a guess"). Kept out of the repo —
# they are output, not source, and they are regenerated whenever a screen
# is next verified.
.preview/
